module.exports = "{\"version\":1,\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q-r-course-t29-1-1\",\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"skill\":\"reading\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"feedbackGroup\":\"r-course-t29-1\",\"difficulty\":2,\"grades\":[9],\"stem\":\"What does a cloudy evening show in these notes?\",\"passage\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The view was blocked\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"The Moon ceased to exist\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The Moon stopped reflecting forever\"}],\"answer\":{\"option\":\"a\",\"display\":\"The view was blocked\"},\"marks\":2,\"estimatedSeconds\":90,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"original\",\"author\":\"Chinese Junior-High English project authors\"},\"review\":\"draft\",\"explanation\":{\"strategy\":\"记录可见形状与遮挡，分清反射光、观察和解释，并指出模型的比例与完整性限制。\",\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"定位原文：“We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared.”\",\"reason\":\"blocked the view只说明观察受阻，下一句明确不把云天当作月球消失的证明。\"},{\"text\":\"核对选项：“The view was blocked”。\",\"reason\":\"把这处线索放回全文，答案没有扩大原文可以支持的范围。\"}],\"distractors\":[{\"option\":\"b\",\"reason\":\"看不见不等于月球不存在。\"},{\"option\":\"c\",\"reason\":\"云遮挡不能证明月球永不再反射光。\"}],\"pitfall\":\"看不见不等于不存在；外观变化不等于拆补月球，模型有用也不等于真实完整。\",\"visual\":{\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"title\":\"原文证据 → 答案\",\"segments\":[{\"text\":\"We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"线索 1\"},{\"text\":\"The view was blocked\",\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"与问题相对应的意思\"}],\"caption\":\"核对线索表达的事实与选项表达的意思，不能只匹配重复的词。\"},\"transfer\":\"遮住选项，用自己的话回答这个问题，再回到原文检查。\"},\"visualMission\":{\"title\":\"地球、太空与探索：读懂信息与用意\",\"subtitle\":\"读题定位 → 原文证据 → 排除干扰\",\"boards\":[{\"id\":\"evidence-0\",\"title\":\"搭一条证据链\",\"instruction\":\"先读问题，点选原文线索。接对以后再看结论。\",\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"diagram\":\"evidence\",\"slots\":[{\"id\":\"proof\",\"label\":\"问题 → 原文线索 → 结论\",\"text\":\"What does a cloudy evening show in these notes?\",\"answer\":\"proof\",\"reason\":\"定位原文：“clouds blocked the view” 这一处直接提供回答问题所需的信息或推断依据。\",\"hint\":\"相近的词或出现过的数字不一定回答本题；推断也必须有原文支持。\"}],\"chips\":[{\"id\":\"clue-1\",\"text\":\"We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared.\"},{\"id\":\"clue-0\",\"text\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings.\"},{\"id\":\"proof\",\"text\":\"clouds blocked the view\"}],\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\",\"conclusion\":\"The view was blocked\"},{\"id\":\"evidence-1\",\"title\":\"搭一条证据链\",\"instruction\":\"先读问题，点选原文线索。接对以后再看结论。\",\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"diagram\":\"evidence\",\"slots\":[{\"id\":\"proof\",\"label\":\"问题 → 原文线索 → 结论\",\"text\":\"Why can we see the Moon?\",\"answer\":\"proof\",\"reason\":\"定位原文：“sunlight reflected from it” 这一处直接提供回答问题所需的信息或推断依据。\",\"hint\":\"相近的词或出现过的数字不一定回答本题；推断也必须有原文支持。\"}],\"chips\":[{\"id\":\"clue-1\",\"text\":\"We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view.\"},{\"id\":\"proof\",\"text\":\"sunlight reflected from it\"},{\"id\":\"clue-0\",\"text\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings.\"}],\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\",\"conclusion\":\"It reflects sunlight\"},{\"id\":\"evidence-2\",\"title\":\"搭一条证据链\",\"instruction\":\"先读问题，点选原文线索。接对以后再看结论。\",\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"diagram\":\"evidence\",\"slots\":[{\"id\":\"proof\",\"label\":\"问题 → 原文线索 → 结论\",\"text\":\"What warning can a classroom model need?\",\"answer\":\"proof\",\"reason\":\"定位原文：“sizes or distances are not to scale” 这一处直接提供回答问题所需的信息或推断依据。\",\"hint\":\"相近的词或出现过的数字不一定回答本题；推断也必须有原文支持。\"}],\"chips\":[{\"id\":\"clue-1\",\"text\":\"We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view.\"},{\"id\":\"clue-0\",\"text\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings.\"},{\"id\":\"proof\",\"text\":\"sizes or distances are not to scale\"}],\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\",\"conclusion\":\"Sizes or distances may not be to scale\"}],\"sourceIds\":[\"q-r-course-t29-1-1\",\"q-r-course-t29-1-2\",\"q-r-course-t29-1-3\",\"q-r-course-t29-1-4\"],\"workshop\":{\"kind\":\"proof\",\"navigationLabel\":\"任务\",\"applicationStyle\":\"cards\",\"title\":\"做观月记录：所见、解释与模型边界\",\"instruction\":\"从清晰和遮挡的画面开始；连接原句核对反光、外观与模型，别把看不见当不存在。\",\"items\":[{\"id\":\"moon-1\",\"label\":\"先看画面：哪里还能记录月亮轮廓\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"Which picture shows a Moon shape that can be drawn?\",\"answer\":\"Picture A: a visible crescent Moon.\",\"reason\":\"左图能看到月牙轮廓，可记录这幅画里可见的形状；右图被云遮住。插画没有日期，不能用它推算某晚的月相。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"clear\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"blocked\",\"text\":\"Picture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"右图只有遮住视野的云，没有可见月亮轮廓；不能凭空补画成真实观察。\"},{\"id\":\"clear\",\"text\":\"Picture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"左图能看到月牙轮廓，可记录这幅画里可见的形状；右图被云遮住。插画没有日期，不能用它推算某晚的月相。\"},{\"id\":\"scale\",\"text\":\"The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"模型比例警告不说明两幅天空插画中哪幅能看见轮廓。\"}],\"sourceArt\":{\"asset\":\"lesson-moon-views\",\"alt\":\"两幅原创虚构夜空插画：左侧可见一弯月牙，右侧云层遮挡同一片天空，看不到月亮轮廓。只比较视野，不给出观测日期，也不表示月球消失。\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"clear\",\"label\":\"图片A\"},{\"id\":\"blocked\",\"label\":\"图片B\"}]}},{\"id\":\"moon-2\",\"label\":\"换个条件：云遮挡，该怎样记\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"Which picture matches a blocked view, rather than a missing Moon?\",\"answer\":\"Picture B: record the cloud-blocked view without claiming the Moon disappeared.\",\"reason\":\"右图没有可见轮廓，因为云遮住视野。配上原文did not...proof，就能区分没看见与证明不存在；左图的月牙不能替右图编一条观测形状。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"blocked\"],[\"cloud\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"clear\",\"text\":\"Picture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"左图视野通畅，不能匹配被云遮挡的记录。\"},{\"id\":\"cloud\",\"text\":\"We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"右图没有可见轮廓，因为云遮住视野。配上原文did not...proof，就能区分没看见与证明不存在；左图的月牙不能替右图编一条观测形状。\"},{\"id\":\"blocked\",\"text\":\"Picture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"右图没有可见轮廓，因为云遮住视野。配上原文did not...proof，就能区分没看见与证明不存在；左图的月牙不能替右图编一条观测形状。\"},{\"id\":\"pieces\",\"text\":\"Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"这一句排除月球被拆掉又补回，不是本题云遮视野的直接记录。\"}],\"evidenceLabels\":[\"选出被云遮挡的图\",\"核对不能证明消失\"],\"sourceArt\":{\"asset\":\"lesson-moon-views\",\"alt\":\"两幅原创虚构夜空插画：左侧可见一弯月牙，右侧云层遮挡同一片天空，看不到月亮轮廓。只比较视野，不给出观测日期，也不表示月球消失。\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"clear\",\"label\":\"图片A\"},{\"id\":\"blocked\",\"label\":\"图片B\"}]}},{\"id\":\"moon-3\",\"label\":\"笔记留什么：时间、形状和遮挡\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"What do the students include in their notes?\",\"answer\":\"The time, visible shape and any cloud-blocked view.\",\"reason\":\"wrote down后是时间与可见形状，and we noted补充云遮挡。看不清也要如实记条件，不能把这一晚删除后假装每晚都看得清。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"record\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"place\",\"text\":\"Our class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"地点安全和几个晚上限定观察范围，没有列齐三项记录内容。\"},{\"id\":\"record\",\"text\":\"We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"wrote down后是时间与可见形状，and we noted补充云遮挡。看不清也要如实记条件，不能把这一晚删除后假装每晚都看得清。\"},{\"id\":\"light\",\"text\":\"The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"反射阳光是解释，不是本题的时间、可见形状和遮挡条件。\"}]},{\"id\":\"moon-4\",\"label\":\"亮着不等于自己发光，回文找依据\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"Why can we see the Moon?\",\"answer\":\"We see sunlight reflected from it; it does not make visible light like the Sun.\",\"reason\":\"分号两边相互配合：前半句否定像太阳那样自己发出可见光，后半句说看见的是反射的阳光。不能从画面很亮推成自身发光。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"light\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"drawing\",\"text\":\"A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"画图记录外观，没有解释可见光来自哪里。\"},{\"id\":\"light\",\"text\":\"The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"分号两边相互配合：前半句否定像太阳那样自己发出可见光，后半句说看见的是反射的阳光。不能从画面很亮推成自身发光。\"},{\"id\":\"pieces\",\"text\":\"Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"月亮外观变化不等于增减碎块，这句没有直接回答光的来源。\"}]},{\"id\":\"moon-5\",\"label\":\"形状变了，就是被拆掉又补上吗\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"Does the changing appearance mean pieces are removed and replaced?\",\"answer\":\"No. A changing appearance does not mean pieces of the Moon are removed and replaced.\",\"reason\":\"does not mean明确否定外观变化等于月球被拆补。原文也没有给出日期或周期，不能借这句算出某一晚具体月相。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"pieces\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"record\",\"text\":\"We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"记录可见形状不是认定月球本体在被切掉或加回。\"},{\"id\":\"pieces\",\"text\":\"Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"does not mean明确否定外观变化等于月球被拆补。原文也没有给出日期或周期，不能借这句算出某一晚具体月相。\"},{\"id\":\"cloud\",\"text\":\"We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"云遮挡不证明消失，但本题直接问外观改变是否等于增减碎块。\"}]},{\"id\":\"moon-6\",\"label\":\"画外观与做模型，作用相同吗\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"How do a drawing and a model have different jobs here?\",\"answer\":\"A drawing records the visible shape; a model helps explore an explanation.\",\"reason\":\"while把两个作用并列对照：drawing记录看到的形状，model帮助探索为什么外观变化。画得像，不等于已经解释了原因。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"drawing\"],[\"separate\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"separate\",\"text\":\"Our teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"while把两个作用并列对照：drawing记录看到的形状，model帮助探索为什么外观变化。画得像，不等于已经解释了原因。\"},{\"id\":\"light\",\"text\":\"The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"反射阳光是一条科学解释，但没有区分画图与模型的不同作用。\"},{\"id\":\"drawing\",\"text\":\"A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"while把两个作用并列对照：drawing记录看到的形状，model帮助探索为什么外观变化。画得像，不等于已经解释了原因。\"}],\"evidenceLabels\":[\"找画图与模型的作用\",\"接上观察和解释的区分\"]},{\"id\":\"moon-7\",\"label\":\"比例不真实，还缺什么提示\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"What should accompany a model that is not to scale?\",\"answer\":\"Labels and a warning that sizes or distances are not to scale.\",\"reason\":\"needs同时要求labels与warning；sizes or distances说明大小或距离可能不按真实比例。模型摆得整齐也不能省略这个说明。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"scale\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"aim\",\"text\":\"Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"这是整篇探索方法的概括，没有直接列出标记与比例警告。\"},{\"id\":\"scale\",\"text\":\"The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"needs同时要求labels与warning；sizes or distances说明大小或距离可能不按真实比例。模型摆得整齐也不能省略这个说明。\"},{\"id\":\"record\",\"text\":\"We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"观测时间和云遮挡是日志内容，不能替代模型比例说明。\"}]},{\"id\":\"moon-8\",\"label\":\"台灯加小球，有用就等于完整吗\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"Is the small-ball-and-lamp model a complete copy?\",\"answer\":\"No. It is useful for thinking, but not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system.\",\"reason\":\"but把有用与并不完整同时保留。否定完整复制，不等于否定模型所有价值；能帮助思考，也不能冒充真实系统。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"copy\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"pieces\",\"text\":\"Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"外观不等于拆补，不能单独判断台灯小球模型是否完整。\"},{\"id\":\"copy\",\"text\":\"A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"but把有用与并不完整同时保留。否定完整复制，不等于否定模型所有价值；能帮助思考，也不能冒充真实系统。\"},{\"id\":\"place\",\"text\":\"Our class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"观察地点安全与模型复制了多少真实关系是两件事。\"}]},{\"id\":\"moon-9\",\"label\":\"能拿小球间距算真实距离吗\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"Can this text supply an exact Earth-Moon distance from the model?\",\"answer\":\"No. It provides no measurements, and a not-to-scale model cannot supply them.\",\"reason\":\"原文提醒大小或距离可能不成比例，又说小球台灯并非完整复制。没有实际测量值，不能量一量画面就冒充真实距离。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"scale\"],[\"copy\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"copy\",\"text\":\"A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"原文提醒大小或距离可能不成比例，又说小球台灯并非完整复制。没有实际测量值，不能量一量画面就冒充真实距离。\"},{\"id\":\"place\",\"text\":\"Our class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"几个晚上和安全地点没有提供地月距离，不能用观察范围换出真实测量值。\"},{\"id\":\"scale\",\"text\":\"The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"原文提醒大小或距离可能不成比例，又说小球台灯并非完整复制。没有实际测量值，不能量一量画面就冒充真实距离。\"}],\"evidenceLabels\":[\"核对比例警告\",\"保留模型不完整的限制\"]},{\"id\":\"moon-10\",\"label\":\"主旨：有记录、有模型，还要有边界\",\"sourceStyle\":\"cards\",\"sourceTitle\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\",\"prompt\":\"What makes exploration careful in this journal?\",\"answer\":\"Careful notes, useful models and clear statements of their limits.\",\"reason\":\"结尾并列三项，不只要画得漂亮或做出一个模型。前面的云遮挡与比例警告，都在示范怎样保留证据边界。\",\"hint\":\"先说看到了什么，再查原文怎样解释；看不清、反光和模型局限，要分别核对。\",\"material\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\\n\\nOriginal picture practice (separate from the class journal):\\nPicture A shows a visible crescent Moon in an unblocked patch of sky.\\nPicture B shows clouds blocking that part of the view; no Moon shape is visible.\\nThese fictional pictures have no observation dates and do not prove that the Moon disappeared or changed its light source.\\nThe pictures compare visibility, not successive measured lunar phases. The text gives no exact dates, phase periods, sizes or distances.\",\"evidenceGroups\":[[\"aim\"],[\"record\"]],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"record\",\"text\":\"We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"结尾并列三项，不只要画得漂亮或做出一个模型。前面的云遮挡与比例警告，都在示范怎样保留证据边界。\"},{\"id\":\"pieces\",\"text\":\"Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\",\"correct\":false,\"reason\":\"这是被排除的一种误解，不能单独覆盖记录、模型与局限这三个要求。\"},{\"id\":\"aim\",\"text\":\"Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\",\"correct\":true,\"reason\":\"结尾并列三项，不只要画得漂亮或做出一个模型。前面的云遮挡与比例警告，都在示范怎样保留证据边界。\"}],\"evidenceLabels\":[\"找全探索的三个要求\",\"接上如实记录的例子\"]}],\"applicationIds\":[\"q-r-course-t29-1-3\",\"q-r-course-t29-1-4\"],\"transfer\":{\"id\":\"individual-r-course-t29-transfer\",\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"skill\":\"reading\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"difficulty\":2,\"grades\":[9],\"stem\":\"Which report keeps both the observation and the model honest?\",\"passage\":\"A FICTIONAL CLUB JOURNAL\\nFrom a safe viewing place, Mei draws the Moon's visible outline on one evening. On another evening, thick cloud blocks the view, so she writes 'view blocked' without inventing an outline or deleting the entry. The teacher uses a labelled ball-and-lamp model to explore appearances and explains that sizes and distances are not to scale. The model leaves out details of the real Earth-Moon system. A drawing records what was seen; a model helps examine an explanation. The class should keep both the observations and the model's limitations clear. No exact dates or distances are supplied.\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Separate the drawing from the explanation, but remove the cloudy entry and measure the model to report the real Earth-Moon distance.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep the blocked-view entry, separate the drawing from the explanation, and state that the model is incomplete and not to scale.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep the blocked-view entry and the scale warning, but label the drawing as a complete explanation of why appearances change.\"}],\"answer\":{\"option\":\"b\",\"display\":\"Keep the blocked-view entry, separate the drawing from the explanation, and state that the model is incomplete and not to scale.\"},\"marks\":2,\"estimatedSeconds\":110,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"original\",\"author\":\"Chinese Junior-High English project authors\"},\"review\":\"draft\",\"explanation\":{\"strategy\":\"分别核对观测记录、画图作用和模型边界；一项正确不能抵消另一项越界。\",\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"保留云遮挡那一晚的记录，不补造轮廓，也不删掉不清楚的观察。\",\"reason\":\"原文写明view blocked；缺少清晰视野不是没有观察条件值得记录。\"},{\"text\":\"图画只记所见轮廓，模型用来探索解释，并注明不完整、不按真实比例。\",\"reason\":\"原文区分两者作用，也明确没有日期或距离；不能量模型冒充真实地月距离。\"}],\"distractors\":[{\"option\":\"c\",\"reason\":\"保留遮挡记录与比例提醒都对，却把记录轮廓的图画说成完整成因解释；画得出形状不等于解释了变化。\"},{\"option\":\"a\",\"reason\":\"区分图画与解释正确，却删掉云遮挡记录，还从不成比例模型计算真实距离；两项都越过原文。\"}],\"pitfall\":\"看不清也要如实记录；模型有用，不等于能提供没有给出的真实测量值。\",\"visual\":{\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"title\":\"记录、解释、局限分开放\",\"segments\":[{\"text\":\"Cloud: view blocked\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"保留条件，不编轮廓\"},{\"text\":\"Drawing: visible outline\",\"role\":\"neutral\",\"note\":\"记录所见\"},{\"text\":\"Model: explore why\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"帮助解释\"},{\"text\":\"Not to scale · incomplete\",\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"不能当真实测量\"}],\"caption\":\"这四项属于同一份谨慎报告；缺少清晰视野，不是删掉记录的理由。\"},\"transfer\":\"如果后来某晚看得很清楚，为什么也要保留先前被云遮挡的记录？\"}}}}},{\"id\":\"q-r-course-t29-1-2\",\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"skill\":\"reading\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"feedbackGroup\":\"r-course-t29-1\",\"difficulty\":2,\"grades\":[9],\"stem\":\"Why can we see the Moon?\",\"passage\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"It makes light like the Sun\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A new piece is added each night\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"It reflects sunlight\"}],\"answer\":{\"option\":\"c\",\"display\":\"It reflects sunlight\"},\"marks\":2,\"estimatedSeconds\":90,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"original\",\"author\":\"Chinese Junior-High English project authors\"},\"review\":\"draft\",\"explanation\":{\"strategy\":\"记录可见形状与遮挡，分清反射光、观察和解释，并指出模型的比例与完整性限制。\",\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"定位原文：“The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it.”\",\"reason\":\"分号前排除像太阳那样自发可见光，分号后给出看见月亮的原因：反射阳光。\"},{\"text\":\"核对选项：“It reflects sunlight”。\",\"reason\":\"把这处线索放回全文，答案没有扩大原文可以支持的范围。\"}],\"distractors\":[{\"option\":\"a\",\"reason\":\"原文明说不是像太阳那样自己发出可见光。\"},{\"option\":\"b\",\"reason\":\"形状变化不是每晚添一块月球。\"}],\"pitfall\":\"看不见不等于不存在；外观变化不等于拆补月球，模型有用也不等于真实完整。\",\"visual\":{\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"title\":\"原文证据 → 答案\",\"segments\":[{\"text\":\"The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"线索 1\"},{\"text\":\"It reflects sunlight\",\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"与问题相对应的意思\"}],\"caption\":\"核对线索表达的事实与选项表达的意思，不能只匹配重复的词。\"},\"transfer\":\"遮住选项，用自己的话回答这个问题，再回到原文检查。\"}},{\"id\":\"q-r-course-t29-1-3\",\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"skill\":\"reading\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"feedbackGroup\":\"r-course-t29-1\",\"difficulty\":2,\"grades\":[9],\"stem\":\"What warning can a classroom model need?\",\"passage\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The lamp is the real Sun\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Sizes or distances may not be to scale\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"It is a perfect copy in every detail\"}],\"answer\":{\"option\":\"b\",\"display\":\"Sizes or distances may not be to scale\"},\"marks\":2,\"estimatedSeconds\":90,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"original\",\"author\":\"Chinese Junior-High English project authors\"},\"review\":\"draft\",\"explanation\":{\"strategy\":\"记录可见形状与遮挡，分清反射光、观察和解释，并指出模型的比例与完整性限制。\",\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"定位原文：“The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale.”\",\"reason\":\"needs并列标记与比例提醒；小球台灯虽有用，也不是地月系统的完整复制。\"},{\"text\":\"核对选项：“Sizes or distances may not be to scale”。\",\"reason\":\"把这处线索放回全文，答案没有扩大原文可以支持的范围。\"}],\"distractors\":[{\"option\":\"a\",\"reason\":\"台灯只是模型中的光源，不是真实太阳。\"},{\"option\":\"c\",\"reason\":\"文中明确小球模型不是完整复制。\"}],\"pitfall\":\"看不见不等于不存在；外观变化不等于拆补月球，模型有用也不等于真实完整。\",\"visual\":{\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"title\":\"原文证据 → 答案\",\"segments\":[{\"text\":\"The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"线索 1\"},{\"text\":\"Sizes or distances may not be to scale\",\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"与问题相对应的意思\"}],\"caption\":\"核对线索表达的事实与选项表达的意思，不能只匹配重复的词。\"},\"transfer\":\"遮住选项，用自己的话回答这个问题，再回到原文检查。\"}},{\"id\":\"q-r-course-t29-1-4\",\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"skill\":\"reading\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"feedbackGroup\":\"r-course-t29-1\",\"difficulty\":2,\"grades\":[9],\"stem\":\"What does careful exploration require?\",\"passage\":\"LOOKING AT THE MOON CAREFULLY\\nOur class observed the Moon from a safe viewing place over several evenings. We wrote down the time and the visible shape, and we noted when clouds blocked the view. We did not record a cloudy evening as proof that the Moon had disappeared. The Moon does not produce its own visible light like the Sun; we see sunlight reflected from it. Its changing appearance during a month does not mean that a piece of the Moon is being removed and replaced.\\nOur teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation. A drawing can record the shape we see, while a model may help us explore why appearances change. The model needs labels and a warning when sizes or distances are not to scale. A small ball beside a lamp is useful for thinking, but it is not a complete copy of the Earth-Moon system. Good exploration includes careful notes, useful models and clear statements about what those models leave out.\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Distinguishing observations and explanations\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Calling every drawing a full explanation\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignoring evenings without a clear view\"}],\"answer\":{\"option\":\"a\",\"display\":\"Distinguishing observations and explanations\"},\"marks\":2,\"estimatedSeconds\":90,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"original\",\"author\":\"Chinese Junior-High English project authors\"},\"review\":\"draft\",\"explanation\":{\"strategy\":\"记录可见形状与遮挡，分清反射光、观察和解释，并指出模型的比例与完整性限制。\",\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"定位原文：“Our teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation.”\",\"reason\":\"drawing记录所见形状，model帮助探索原因；不能把图画、解释和完整复制混为一谈。\"},{\"text\":\"核对选项：“Distinguishing observations and explanations”。\",\"reason\":\"把这处线索放回全文，答案没有扩大原文可以支持的范围。\"}],\"distractors\":[{\"option\":\"b\",\"reason\":\"记录外观和解释成因并不是同一件事。\"},{\"option\":\"c\",\"reason\":\"云遮挡也应记在观测条件中，而非忽略。\"}],\"pitfall\":\"看不见不等于不存在；外观变化不等于拆补月球，模型有用也不等于真实完整。\",\"visual\":{\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"title\":\"原文证据 → 答案\",\"segments\":[{\"text\":\"Our teacher asked us to separate observation from explanation.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"线索 1\"},{\"text\":\"Distinguishing observations and explanations\",\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"与问题相对应的意思\"}],\"caption\":\"核对线索表达的事实与选项表达的意思，不能只匹配重复的词。\"},\"transfer\":\"遮住选项，用自己的话回答这个问题，再回到原文检查。\"}},{\"id\":\"q-r-course-t29-2-1\",\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"skill\":\"reading\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"feedbackGroup\":\"r-course-t29-2\",\"difficulty\":2,\"grades\":[9],\"stem\":\"What is the mission’s status?\",\"passage\":\"A MISSION ON PAPER\\nOur science club designed a fictional mission to study a distant rocky world. We did not choose a real launch date or claim that our paper design could fly. First, we decided what question the mission should answer. We wanted to compare surface pictures from two areas, so a camera was more important to our plan than a device for collecting sound. We then considered power, communication and the limits of the pictures.\\nA clear image would not tell us everything about the material beneath the surface. Nor would one interesting shape prove that life had been found. Our report lists what further evidence would be needed before making a stronger claim. Because our map is invented, every place name is marked as fictional. The project helped us practise asking a focused question and matching a tool to it. Space exploration can inspire large hopes, but a useful investigation still needs precise aims, honest uncertainty and a way to explain how the evidence supports a conclusion.\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A fictional design project\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A confirmed real launch\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"An official discovery of life\"}],\"answer\":{\"option\":\"a\",\"display\":\"A fictional design project\"},\"marks\":2,\"estimatedSeconds\":90,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"original\",\"author\":\"Chinese Junior-High English project authors\"},\"review\":\"draft\",\"explanation\":{\"strategy\":\"记录可见形状与遮挡，分清反射光、观察和解释，并指出模型的比例与完整性限制。\",\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"定位原文：“designed a fictional mission”\",\"reason\":\"把线索与题目中的人物、时间和行为对应起来，再得出判断。\"},{\"text\":\"核对选项：“A fictional design project”。\",\"reason\":\"把这处线索放回全文，答案没有扩大原文可以支持的范围。\"}],\"distractors\":[{\"option\":\"b\",\"reason\":\"文中没有真实发射日期。\"},{\"option\":\"c\",\"reason\":\"项目没有宣布发现生命。\"}],\"pitfall\":\"看不见不等于不存在；外观变化不等于拆补月球，模型有用也不等于真实完整。\",\"visual\":{\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"title\":\"原文证据 → 答案\",\"segments\":[{\"text\":\"designed a fictional mission\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"线索 1\"},{\"text\":\"A fictional design project\",\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"与问题相对应的意思\"}],\"caption\":\"核对线索表达的事实与选项表达的意思，不能只匹配重复的词。\"},\"transfer\":\"遮住选项，用自己的话回答这个问题，再回到原文检查。\"}},{\"id\":\"q-r-course-t29-2-2\",\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"skill\":\"reading\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"feedbackGroup\":\"r-course-t29-2\",\"difficulty\":2,\"grades\":[9],\"stem\":\"Why is a camera important?\",\"passage\":\"A MISSION ON PAPER\\nOur science club designed a fictional mission to study a distant rocky world. We did not choose a real launch date or claim that our paper design could fly. First, we decided what question the mission should answer. We wanted to compare surface pictures from two areas, so a camera was more important to our plan than a device for collecting sound. We then considered power, communication and the limits of the pictures.\\nA clear image would not tell us everything about the material beneath the surface. Nor would one interesting shape prove that life had been found. Our report lists what further evidence would be needed before making a stronger claim. Because our map is invented, every place name is marked as fictional. The project helped us practise asking a focused question and matching a tool to it. Space exploration can inspire large hopes, but a useful investigation still needs precise aims, honest uncertainty and a way to explain how the evidence supports a conclusion.\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The team wants only sound recordings\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A camera explains everything below the surface\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The question involves comparing surface pictures\"}],\"answer\":{\"option\":\"c\",\"display\":\"The question involves comparing surface pictures\"},\"marks\":2,\"estimatedSeconds\":90,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"original\",\"author\":\"Chinese Junior-High English project authors\"},\"review\":\"draft\",\"explanation\":{\"strategy\":\"记录可见形状与遮挡，分清反射光、观察和解释，并指出模型的比例与完整性限制。\",\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"定位原文：“compare surface pictures from two areas”\",\"reason\":\"把线索与题目中的人物、时间和行为对应起来，再得出判断。\"},{\"text\":\"核对选项：“The question involves comparing surface pictures”。\",\"reason\":\"把这处线索放回全文，答案没有扩大原文可以支持的范围。\"}],\"distractors\":[{\"option\":\"a\",\"reason\":\"团队的问题不是仅记录声音。\"},{\"option\":\"b\",\"reason\":\"后文说明表面图像不能揭示地下全部情况。\"}],\"pitfall\":\"看不见不等于不存在；外观变化不等于拆补月球，模型有用也不等于真实完整。\",\"visual\":{\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"title\":\"原文证据 → 答案\",\"segments\":[{\"text\":\"compare surface pictures from two areas\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"线索 1\"},{\"text\":\"The question involves comparing surface pictures\",\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"与问题相对应的意思\"}],\"caption\":\"核对线索表达的事实与选项表达的意思，不能只匹配重复的词。\"},\"transfer\":\"遮住选项，用自己的话回答这个问题，再回到原文检查。\"}},{\"id\":\"q-r-course-t29-2-3\",\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"skill\":\"reading\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"feedbackGroup\":\"r-course-t29-2\",\"difficulty\":2,\"grades\":[9],\"stem\":\"Which conclusion would be premature from one interesting shape?\",\"passage\":\"A MISSION ON PAPER\\nOur science club designed a fictional mission to study a distant rocky world. We did not choose a real launch date or claim that our paper design could fly. First, we decided what question the mission should answer. We wanted to compare surface pictures from two areas, so a camera was more important to our plan than a device for collecting sound. We then considered power, communication and the limits of the pictures.\\nA clear image would not tell us everything about the material beneath the surface. Nor would one interesting shape prove that life had been found. Our report lists what further evidence would be needed before making a stronger claim. Because our map is invented, every place name is marked as fictional. The project helped us practise asking a focused question and matching a tool to it. Space exploration can inspire large hopes, but a useful investigation still needs precise aims, honest uncertainty and a way to explain how the evidence supports a conclusion.\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Further evidence could be useful\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Life has been found\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The image can lead to a new question\"}],\"answer\":{\"option\":\"b\",\"display\":\"Life has been found\"},\"marks\":2,\"estimatedSeconds\":90,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"original\",\"author\":\"Chinese Junior-High English project authors\"},\"review\":\"draft\",\"explanation\":{\"strategy\":\"记录可见形状与遮挡，分清反射光、观察和解释，并指出模型的比例与完整性限制。\",\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"定位原文：“Nor would one interesting shape prove that life had been found.”\",\"reason\":\"把线索与题目中的人物、时间和行为对应起来，再得出判断。\"},{\"text\":\"核对选项：“Life has been found”。\",\"reason\":\"把这处线索放回全文，答案没有扩大原文可以支持的范围。\"}],\"distractors\":[{\"option\":\"a\",\"reason\":\"继续寻找证据是合理的，原文反对的是缺乏证据就宣布结论。\"},{\"option\":\"c\",\"reason\":\"图像可以引出新问题，但不能单凭一个形状断定已发现生命。\"}],\"pitfall\":\"看不见不等于不存在；外观变化不等于拆补月球，模型有用也不等于真实完整。\",\"visual\":{\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"title\":\"原文证据 → 答案\",\"segments\":[{\"text\":\"Nor would one interesting shape prove that life had been found.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"线索 1\"},{\"text\":\"Life has been found\",\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"与问题相对应的意思\"}],\"caption\":\"核对线索表达的事实与选项表达的意思，不能只匹配重复的词。\"},\"transfer\":\"遮住选项，用自己的话回答这个问题，再回到原文检查。\"}},{\"id\":\"q-r-course-t29-2-4\",\"topicId\":\"r-course-t29\",\"skill\":\"reading\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"feedbackGroup\":\"r-course-t29-2\",\"difficulty\":2,\"grades\":[9],\"stem\":\"What makes an investigation useful?\",\"passage\":\"A MISSION ON PAPER\\nOur science club designed a fictional mission to study a distant rocky world. We did not choose a real launch date or claim that our paper design could fly. First, we decided what question the mission should answer. We wanted to compare surface pictures from two areas, so a camera was more important to our plan than a device for collecting sound. We then considered power, communication and the limits of the pictures.\\nA clear image would not tell us everything about the material beneath the surface. Nor would one interesting shape prove that life had been found. Our report lists what further evidence would be needed before making a stronger claim. Because our map is invented, every place name is marked as fictional. The project helped us practise asking a focused question and matching a tool to it. Space exploration can inspire large hopes, but a useful investigation still needs precise aims, honest uncertainty and a way to explain how the evidence supports a conclusion.\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Focused aims and evidence with stated limits\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Invented places presented as real\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Large hopes without a clear question\"}],\"answer\":{\"option\":\"a\",\"display\":\"Focused aims and evidence with stated limits\"},\"marks\":2,\"estimatedSeconds\":90,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"original\",\"author\":\"Chinese Junior-High English project authors\"},\"review\":\"draft\",\"explanation\":{\"strategy\":\"记录可见形状与遮挡，分清反射光、观察和解释，并指出模型的比例与完整性限制。\",\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"定位原文：“precise aims, honest uncertainty”\",\"reason\":\"把线索与题目中的人物、时间和行为对应起来，再得出判断。\"},{\"text\":\"核对选项：“Focused aims and evidence with stated limits”。\",\"reason\":\"把这处线索放回全文，答案没有扩大原文可以支持的范围。\"}],\"distractors\":[{\"option\":\"b\",\"reason\":\"文中明确给虚构地名作标记，不冒充真实地点。\"},{\"option\":\"c\",\"reason\":\"全文强调先提出具体问题，不只依赖宏大愿望。\"}],\"pitfall\":\"看不见不等于不存在；外观变化不等于拆补月球，模型有用也不等于真实完整。\",\"visual\":{\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"title\":\"原文证据 → 答案\",\"segments\":[{\"text\":\"precise aims, honest uncertainty\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"note\":\"线索 1\"},{\"text\":\"Focused aims and evidence with stated limits\",\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"与问题相对应的意思\"}],\"caption\":\"核对线索表达的事实与选项表达的意思，不能只匹配重复的词。\"},\"transfer\":\"遮住选项，用自己的话回答这个问题，再回到原文检查。\"}}]}";
